{"base_rate":0.41601049868766404,"brier":0.13335459317585302,"bss":0.4510931528018999,"bss_hi":0.5293206779089338,"bss_lo":0.36269081792772434,"chart":{"base":[601.4,113.6],"fp":[260.8,282.3],"lead":"62,232.6 272,201.2 482,147.8 692,66.8","note":{"base":"skill 0.45 — higher than 81% of cities","fp":"low end +6pp, high end +13pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.3 °C — better than 33% of cities","rel":"promised 0% → rained 6%; promised 100% → rained 89%"},"rel":"64.3,439.5 242.7,315.9 581.5,180.3 689.5,82.5"},"country":"DE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.08782152230971131,"ess":354.9642777302465,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Munich</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Munich rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 5 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (100%), believe about\n<b>89%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>6%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 762 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nMUNCHEN-NYMPHENBURG, 6.3 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.45, ranked 25 of\n134 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(11&ndash;52) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>6%</b></td><td class='num'>293</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>12%</td><td class='num'><b>24%</b></td><td class='num'>84</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'><b>46%</b></td><td class='num'>80</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>75%</td><td class='num'><b>55%</b></td><td class='num'>71</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>92%</td><td class='num'><b>80%</b></td><td class='num'>56</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>100%</td><td class='num'><b>89%</b></td><td class='num'>178</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">5 of 6 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Munich</b> <span class=\"muted\">DE</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">5 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.45</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>11&ndash;52\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 134</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>762 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Munich &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Munich\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"58\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">0%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"386\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">0%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"146.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"146.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"291.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"291.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"146.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">25%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"295.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">25%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"235.0\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"235.0\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"200.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"200.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">50%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"204.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">50%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"323.5\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"323.5\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"109.0\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"109.0\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"323.5\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">75%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"113.0\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">75%</text><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"412\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"18\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\"/><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"412\" y=\"399\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\">100%</text><text class=\"chart-axis\" x=\"49\" y=\"22\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"end\">100%</text><polygon class=\"chart-band\" points=\"59.304846416382254,378.2730375426621 101.07,308.3333333333333 220.88425,177.25 323.05126760563377,74.3943661971831 383.99607142857144,24.5 410.6078651685394,18.0 410.6078651685394,24.13483146067415 383.99607142857144,70.0 323.05126760563377,146.16901408450704 220.88425,250.05 101.07,360.3333333333333 59.304846416382254,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"230.5721784776903\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"230.5721784776903\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"59.304846416382254,359.6382252559727 101.07,295.33333333333337 220.88425,213.65 323.05126760563377,182.056338028169 383.99607142857144,89.5 410.6078651685394,58.89887640449439\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 6% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 293 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"59.304846416382254\" cy=\"359.6382252559727\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 12%&amp;#10;It rained 24% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 84 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"101.07\" cy=\"295.33333333333337\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 46%&amp;#10;It rained 46% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 80 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"220.88425\" cy=\"213.65\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 75%&amp;#10;It rained 55% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 71 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"323.05126760563377\" cy=\"182.056338028169\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 92%&amp;#10;It rained 80% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 56 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"383.99607142857144\" cy=\"89.5\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 100%&amp;#10;It rained 89% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 178 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"410.6078651685394\" cy=\"58.89887640449439\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(42%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Munich the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.50) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.40).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>50%</td><td class='num'>0.396</td><td class='num'>9.7%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>48%</td><td class='num'>0.420</td><td class='num'>9.1%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>36%</td><td class='num'>0.438</td><td class='num'>10.9%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'>0.501</td><td class='num'>7.0%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":48.13743,"lon":11.57549,"n":762,"n_cities":134,"name":"Munich","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.05,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0036860068259385666,"n":293,"obs":0.06143344709897611,"sig":true},{"hi":0.3,"lo":0.05,"mean":0.12166666666666667,"n":84,"obs":0.23809523809523808,"sig":true},{"hi":0.6420000000000016,"lo":0.3,"mean":0.460125,"n":80,"obs":0.4625,"sig":false},{"hi":0.88,"lo":0.6420000000000016,"mean":0.7487323943661971,"n":71,"obs":0.5492957746478874,"sig":true},{"hi":0.98,"lo":0.88,"mean":0.9208928571428572,"n":56,"obs":0.8035714285714286,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.98,"mean":0.9960674157303372,"n":178,"obs":0.8876404494382022,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":6.3,"provisional":false,"rank":25,"rank_hi":52.02499999999998,"rank_lo":11.0,"reliability":0.010241042176318875,"resolution":0.1167130173673421,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"munich","station":"MUNCHEN-NYMPHENBURG","timezone":"Europe/Berlin"}